  {
   "index": 10,
   "tag": "p×2",
   "landmarks": [
    "role=main"
   ],
   "textLength": 900,
   "text": "What I understand from this is that Evictions occur when a Kubernetes component (a controller, kubelet, etc.) terminates one or more pods on nodes as part of its intended functionality. In other words, Evictions are a feature. Whereas, Pod Disruption is a phenomenon during which one or more pods on nodes can be terminated either intentionally (automatically by a Kubernetes component or manually in",
