   "text": "As I read it, eviction is pod disruption as well. It's initiated by k8s when node resources are exhausted or when the eviction API is used. It's supposed to be a graceful shutdown.\nThe other forms of disruption trigger due to user command (deployment strategy, replica count change, config change) or due to OOM (resource limits) or crash.\n Share\nShare a link to this answer \nCopy linkCC BY-SA 4.0\nSh",
